  "text": "GANGSTAS PARADISE (Sleeper) \u2014 Higgins, Flowers and Downs all trending to play \u2014 lineup set\nDo now: nothing \u2014 lineup is set\nLocks next 24h: none \u2014 first kickoff is Fri 5:00 PM PT (Herbert, Hampton vs KC, S\u00e3o Paulo)\nLineup, by kickoff: Herbert (QB) and Hampton (RB), Fri 5:00 PM PT vs KC \u2014 no news, both in. Chase Brown (RB), Higgins (WR, Q \u2014 heel contusion, limited practice, Taylor calls it minor), Flowers (WR, Q \u2014 lower-body, trending back to full practice), Strange (TE), Tuten (FLEX RB, Q \u2014 lingering illness tag, JAX's real risk is the Rodriguez/Allen committee behind him not his health), Downs (FLEX WR, Q \u2014 calf, \"very minor,\" trending toward off the report), and JAX DEF all kick off Sun 10:00 AM PT. Aubrey (K) closes it out Sun 5:20 PM PT @ NYG. If Higgins is out, start Diggs. If Flowers is out, start Diggs. If Downs is out, start Diggs; if two of Higgins/Flowers/Downs are out, Diggs then Michael Wilson. If Tuten is out, start Woody Marks.\n\nGAME OF THROWS (Yahoo) \u2014 39% underdog vs GIBBBBBYYYY; Stafford opens Thursday in Melbourne, Etienne now the clean lead with Kamara out \u2014 lineup set\nDo now: nothing \u2014 lineup is set\nLocks next 24h: none \u2014 first kickoff is Wed 5:20 PM PT (Myers vs NE)\nLineup, by kickoff: Myers (K), Wed 5:20 PM PT vs NE \u2014 no news, in. Stafford (QB) and 49ers DEF, Thu 5:35 PM PT @ LAR in Melbourne \u2014 Stafford a full camp participant, no news; 49ers DEF stays your weakest starter (4.32 proj) but nothing actionable. Chase Brown (RB), Etienne (RB), Judkins (W/R/T), G. Wilson (WR) and P. Washington (WR) all kick off Sun 10:00 AM PT \u2014 Etienne is the clean NO lead now that Kamara (MCL) is confirmed out about a month; Judkins is entrenched as Cleveland's RB1 over Sampson/Sanders; Brown, G. Wilson, P. Washington have no news. Pickens (WR) and Likely (TE) close it out Sun 5:20 PM PT @ NYG / vs DAL \u2014 no news, both in. No Qs on this roster, no contingencies needed.\n\nFYI: Chase Brown starts for you in both leagues; your JAX DEF (Sleeper) and Judkins' Browns (Yahoo) collide in the same CLE@JAX game; Yahoo opp Arshdeep still carries three Qs (Jeanty-ankle, HC optimistic; Nabers-knee, won't commit to Week 1; LaPorta-hip, back to full practice) and Sleeper opp AdufortheWin84's Henderson (ankle) and Pittman (hamstring, now on PIT) are both trending to play.\nData: Sleeper live \u00b7 Yahoo screenshots from 2026-09-05",
